          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homes, the Shark FlexBreeze is the best battery powered fan: a real pedestal fan for everyday use that keeps running through a night-long outage on low. If you already own Ryobi, Makita or DeWalt batteries, buy that platform's fan as a bare tool instead, and spend the savings on a bigger battery. Makita's DCF203Z is the most efficient for sleeping; DeWalt's DCE512B moves the most air in a hot garage.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, ignore the headline runtime and plan around the medium setting, keep emergency fans charged, and remember that fans cool people, not rooms. When the heat is extreme, a fan is not a substitute for a cooled space.
          </p>
